 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** Committed changes are pushed to browsers via self-hosted WebSockets. Five-second HTTPS polling was rejected for repeated reads and seconds of lag; hosted realtime service was rejected to avoid recurring fees and provider coupling. WebSockets require connection management, reconnect handling, replayable revisions, and reliable publication. See `docs/decisions/websocket-delivery.md`.
